## Erik's Architecture Requirements (from recommendation doc)

From Section 6.2 of Erik's architecture recommendation, v1 must support:

- Per-user soft daily token limits (prevent runaway scripts)
- Per-team monthly hard caps with alerting at 75% and 90%
- Global circuit breaker (disable service if 24-hour spend exceeds threshold)

Mapping to LiteLLM options:

| Requirement | LiteLLM Mechanism | Database Required |
|---|---|---|
| Per-user soft daily token limit | Per-key `tpm_limit` + `max_budget` / `budget_duration: "daily"` | Yes |
| Per-team monthly hard cap | Per-team key `max_budget` + `budget_duration: "monthly"` | Yes |
| Alert at 75% / 90% of budget | LiteLLM budget alert callbacks | Yes |
| Global circuit breaker | Global `rpm_limit` in config + alerting | Partial |

